        # Introduction to Testing

        Testing is a critical process in software development, ensuring software quality and reliability. This report delves into various testing methodologies and techniques, providing a comprehensive overview of how software is rigorously evaluated. We will explore diverse approaches, including black-box, white-box, and gray-box testing, examining their differences and applications.

